Instructions for running a lidar scan and subsequent DEM creation.

Use WSL Terminals only for this routine.
TURN ON THE GANTRY COMPUTER VIA THE BREAKER BOX NEAR GROUND CONTROL.
TURN OFF THE OPTITRACK LEDS!!! Otherwise they interfere with the lidar.

Terminal 1:
===========
# Start the lidar, stream them over ros2
ssh -i .ssh/id_rsa_ansible gantry@192.168.2.99 # SSH into gantry computer
cd gantry_control
./run_roselab_perception.sh

Terminal 2:
===========
# Run remote bagging service
ssh -i .ssh/id_rsa_ansible gantry@192.168.2.99 # SSH into gantry computer
source roselab-perception/ros/install/setup.bash
ros2 run gantry_services gantry_capture_service

Terminal 3:
===========
# Runs the perception ground control service, which triggers/downloads all remote bags of data
source roselab-perception/ros/install/setup.bash
ros2 launch perception_ground_control launch_ground.py

Terminal 4:
===========
# Triggers and downloads a single lidar scan
source roselab-perception/ros/install/setup.bash
cd roselab-perception/scripts
./run_lidar_scan.sh

Terminal 4:
===========
# After taking a lidar scan, you will see a downloaded bag at /mnt/e/perception-data/..., which you supply below as "<PATH TO BAG>"
source roselab-perception/ros/install/setup.bash
cd roselab-perception/scripts
uv run ./run_dem_pipeline.sh <PATH TO BAG>

# The DEM generator will output the results IN THE BAG DIRECTORY SPECIFIED, and uses a stale "+Z UP" vector for its statistics [WARNING].
